#!/usr/bin/env xetal
# HEX1000 with the board's glue, at the glue's ports: the specification
# its circuit (demos/hex1000-board.xir, rtl/hex1000-board.v) must
# reproduce clock for clock. The characters 12+34= arrive one a clock
# from reset, as a serial receiver would hand them over; the machine
# and the glue run 1710 clocks. Line 1: the character given at each
# clock (0: none); line 2: whether a frame was just completed, after
# reset and after each clock; then the eight digit latches, digit 0
# first, a row after reset and after each clock. Run with
# "just demo-lib Hex1000 board".
"hx:" u_se< "Hex1000"
(cs, fs, ds) := hx:CalcRom hx:w_ires ("12+34=", 1710)
cs
fs
ds
